    "The Short Burst method is a redistricting ensemble generation technique that performs a limited number of Markov Chain steps (often using a recombination-based proposal like ReCom) starting from the enacted plan. Instead of running long chains that aim to fully mix the state space, Short Burst chains produce localized perturbations of the original map. This helps create a representative, though not exhaustive, set of nearby plans that satisfy population balance, compactness, and legal constraints—providing a meaningful baseline to evaluate the initial plan’s proximity to fair alternatives."
   ]
  },
